The probes confirm the main issue: under OAS 3.1, an out-of-range integral float such as `9223372036854775808.0` still passes `integer/int64` validation. Plain JSON integers and all four parameter locations pass the boundary checks. The 98 unit tests pass; I’m now comparing legacy CLI output with the pre-change source on four saved baseline runs.
